5.3 Gate P1.1 — Electromagnetic levitation and drag

Inputs [H]: Halbach wavelength λ = 0.1 m; track inductance L_tr and resistance R_tr per unit length; peak surface field B_0. With ω = 2πv/λ and x = R_tr/(ωL_tr):

F_L = \frac{B_0^2}{2\mu_0}\,\frac{1}{1+x^2}, \qquad F_D = \frac{B_0^2}{2\mu_0}\,\frac{x}{1+x^2}, \qquad \frac{L}{D}=\frac{F_L}{F_D}=\frac{v}{v_c}, \qquad v_c=\frac{\lambda R_{tr}}{2\pi L_{tr}}

With the vehicle weight carried by F_L, the drag power is P_D = mg·v/(L/D). The relation L/D = v/v_c is exact inside this circuit model; it is a property of the model, not evidence that a real track achieves it.

Reference domain. v_c ∈ [0.133, 0.533] m/s, which at 8 m/s means L/D ∈ [15, 60]. In this domain v/v_c ≥ 15 and F_L is within 0.5% of its high-speed value.

